# ./run-tests.sh end to end, Windows 11 + RTX 3060, 2026-11-27 (excerpt of 4994 lines)
#
# Environment: ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation\ort-1.32.0 (the version the pin in
# .github/actions/onnx-runtime names), VULKAN_SDK=.validation\vk\sdk,
# OFX_SOURCE_DIR resolved to ./.ofx-ref, nvcc from CUDA 13.0 on PATH, no
# CPU_ONLY, no SANITIZE, no RUN_VALGRIND. Windows route: the .bat runners, one per
# template - all five of them, minimal-vulkan-ofx included.
#
# This is the run after the Vulkan runner gained a contract pass that sets
# OFXPLUGIN_VULKAN_MODE=gpux and asserts the Device label carries the sentence
# saying the word is unrecognised. That pass is 94 checks, so the template's count
# is 899 (118 x 4 + the forced-CPU pass + the misspelt-override pass + the install
# pass + the device-label pass, plus 29 in the policy test and 26 in the device
# suite) and the tree's is 3,017.
#
# This file keeps the section headers, the per-suite counts, the host-profile
# lines, every skip line, the summary block and the exit status; the full log
# (4994 lines) stays in .validation/, which is not tracked. Nothing below was
# edited by hand.

